WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.902
-Thank you very much
to all of you five people.

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:05.038
Thank you.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:08.107
It is Friday, everybody.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:08.107 --> 00:00:10.343
That's a great reaction.

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:11.910
That is -- you don't
understand.

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:16.015
That is a great reaction.
There's only five people here.

00:00:16.015 --> 00:00:18.251
Let's get to the news
and jokes.

00:00:18.251 --> 00:00:21.588
Well, guys, last night was
the start of the NFL season.

00:00:21.588 --> 00:00:23.356
And I got to say, it was kind of
strange to see

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:26.659
a live sport event with
fans in the crowd.

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:28.061
I was a little worried at first

00:00:28.061 --> 00:00:30.496
until I saw the crowd
at the president's rally

00:00:30.496 --> 00:00:32.465
in Michigan last night.

00:00:32.465 --> 00:00:34.334
Yikes!

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:36.836
I need a nasal swab just
from looking at that.

00:00:36.836 --> 00:00:38.371
[ Laughter ]

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:40.406
If you're trying to figure out
how many Bob Woodward tapes

00:00:40.406 --> 00:00:42.742
we need for people to take
COVID seriously,

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:45.411
it appears the answer is
more than 18.

00:00:45.411 --> 00:00:46.880
What are they doing?

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:49.415
Even the cardboard cutouts at
Major League Baseball games

00:00:49.415 --> 00:00:51.518
are more spread out than that.

00:00:51.518 --> 00:00:53.285
Can we see that photo again?

00:00:53.285 --> 00:00:54.887
Wow!

00:00:54.887 --> 00:00:56.322
That's a lot of white people.

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:58.625
Looks like a mosh pit
at a Kenny G concert.

00:00:58.625 --> 00:01:03.129
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:06.098
People --

00:01:06.098 --> 00:01:08.100
Dude, once he goes into
"Songbird," it's like --

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:09.802
Wah!

00:01:09.802 --> 00:01:13.806
[ Vocalizing smooth jazz ]
♪♪

00:01:13.806 --> 00:01:16.976
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:19.412
People are calling last night's
rally --

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:21.781
-Can we do that?

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:23.849
-We should.
-Mosh to Kenny G?

00:01:23.849 --> 00:01:25.685
-I would totally mosh
to Kenny G.

00:01:25.685 --> 00:01:28.521
Last time I tried moshing,
I went to, like,

00:01:28.521 --> 00:01:31.290
I wanna say, one of the later
Lollapaloozas.

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:32.891
And I was like,
"I can handle myself.

00:01:32.891 --> 00:01:34.226
I can mosh.
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:34.226 --> 00:01:35.828
It's cool. I could --
it's totally cool.

00:01:35.828 --> 00:01:37.229
Let's get in there."

00:01:37.229 --> 00:01:39.031
And, dude, I got a boot to the
head, and I was like,

00:01:39.031 --> 00:01:40.700
too old, too old.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:43.336
-I wore Birkenstocks to see
Henry Rollins.

00:01:43.336 --> 00:01:45.237
-No, that was the end of that.
-Never again.

00:01:45.237 --> 00:01:48.074
-You lost three toes.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:48.074 --> 00:01:49.742
-It was like, old guy, old guy
in the mosh pit!

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:53.479
Old guy! Just get the old guy
out. They carried me out.

00:01:53.479 --> 00:01:55.715
That's right, people are
calling last night's rally

00:01:55.715 --> 00:01:57.684
a super spreader event.

00:01:57.684 --> 00:01:58.985
When he heard that,
Trump was like,

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:03.322
"Amazing, even CNN
said it was super."

00:02:03.322 --> 00:02:05.991
And everyone's talking about
this moment from the rally.

00:02:05.991 --> 00:02:08.928
Did you see this yet?
Oh, my goodness.

00:02:08.928 --> 00:02:11.964
So Trump is trying to go through
the history of Michigan,

00:02:11.964 --> 00:02:14.900
but he stumbled over the word
Motown.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:16.068
Check it out.

00:02:16.068 --> 00:02:19.038 line:0%
-Michigan gave us Motang.

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:22.008 line:0%
Gave us Motown.
Give us the Mustang.

00:02:22.008 --> 00:02:26.178
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.178 --> 00:02:27.747
-Mo...
-Motan.

00:02:27.747 --> 00:02:30.483
-"All the Motang's
great artists,

00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:34.020
like Smokey Robinsang,
Marvin Gang,

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:36.589
and the Jacksgang Five.

00:02:38.457 --> 00:02:42.494
Who could forget the great
Motown song,

00:02:42.494 --> 00:02:44.364
"Papa Was a Roping Stone?"

00:02:44.364 --> 00:02:45.931
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.931 --> 00:02:48.634
I'm just going to do a million
of these, man.

00:02:48.634 --> 00:02:49.902
Trump was like,

00:02:49.902 --> 00:02:52.538
"I even love all the rappers
in the Motang Clan."

00:02:52.538 --> 00:02:57.210
[ Laughter ]

00:02:58.844 --> 00:03:02.015
"That's right. Michigan gave us
Heidi Motang,

00:03:02.015 --> 00:03:04.884
Spencer, LC, and of course,
Brody Jenner."

00:03:04.884 --> 00:03:07.786
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.786 --> 00:03:09.421
Later on, Trump said,

00:03:09.421 --> 00:03:13.259
"Motang, of course, began
in the great city of De-twa."

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:15.295
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.295 --> 00:03:17.296
Right after that,
"Yo-semite" National Park

00:03:17.296 --> 00:03:20.533
was like, "Damn, you too?"

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:23.001
Yeah, Trump mispronounced
Motown as Motang.

00:03:23.001 --> 00:03:25.237
It was a simple mistake,
but to prove that he's actually

00:03:25.237 --> 00:03:27.573
a huge fan of Motown,
he released this message.

00:03:27.573 --> 00:03:29.808
Take a look.
-I'm Donald J. Trump,

00:03:29.808 --> 00:03:31.710
here to talk about
all the fantastic artists

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:33.378
that came out of Motown.

00:03:33.378 --> 00:03:36.148 line:0%
Artists like Betty White,

00:03:36.148 --> 00:03:37.917 line:0%
the Burrito Supremes,

00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:40.086 line:0%
Orville Redenbacher,

00:03:40.086 --> 00:03:42.555 line:0%
Marvin
Word Mike Pence Won't Say,

00:03:42.555 --> 00:03:46.258 line:0%
Stevie Wonder, Ray Charles,

00:03:46.258 --> 00:03:48.127 line:0%
Glade Plug-ins,

00:03:48.127 --> 00:03:52.031 line:0%
and my personal favorite,
Eats Domino's.

00:03:52.031 --> 00:03:57.002
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.002 --> 00:03:59.038
-Later in the rally,
Trump mentioned an award

00:03:59.038 --> 00:04:01.040
that he's won in the past that
I didn't really know about.

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:02.041
Watch this.

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:03.576 line:0%
-Well, I was honored
in Michigan.

00:04:03.576 --> 00:04:05.377 line:0%
Does anybody know that?

00:04:05.377 --> 00:04:08.781 line:0%
I was given Man of the Year
award by somebody.

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:10.950
[ Laughter ]

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:13.819
If you --
[ Laughs ]

00:04:13.819 --> 00:04:15.187
-If you don't remember

00:04:15.187 --> 00:04:17.089
the Michigan Man of the Year
Awards, there's a reason.

00:04:17.089 --> 00:04:18.925
They don't exist.

00:04:18.925 --> 00:04:20.659
His staff was like,
"When he's in a bad mood,

00:04:20.659 --> 00:04:22.495
we just give him a trophy with
a post-it note on it.

00:04:22.495 --> 00:04:23.863
Just take it."

00:04:23.863 --> 00:04:25.198
Trump's just making up awards.

00:04:25.198 --> 00:04:26.832
"I was named Michigan's
Man of the Year,

00:04:26.832 --> 00:04:29.969
Wisconsin's
Most Stable Genius,

00:04:29.969 --> 00:04:32.571
and Ohio's Sexiest Man Alive."

00:04:32.571 --> 00:04:35.574
Trump said he was given
the award by somebody.

00:04:35.574 --> 00:04:37.543
Honestly, the only thing
foggier than that claim

00:04:37.543 --> 00:04:39.612
is Andy Reid's
face shield.

00:04:39.612 --> 00:04:42.415
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.415 --> 00:04:44.917
Speaking of awards, the Trump
campaign tried to celebrate

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:48.187
the president's Nobel Prize
nomination on Facebook,

00:04:48.187 --> 00:04:50.456
but they had some trouble
with the spelling.

00:04:50.456 --> 00:04:52.325
This is real.
Look at what they posted.

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:56.061 line:0%
They spelled Nobel wrong.
-No.

00:04:56.061 --> 00:04:57.763 line:0%
-That is real.
-No.

00:04:57.763 --> 00:04:59.865 line:0%
-They spelled Nobel --

00:04:59.865 --> 00:05:01.867 line:0%
Trump saw that and was like,
"You idiots.

00:05:01.867 --> 00:05:04.137 line:0%
It's prize with an "s."

00:05:04.137 --> 00:05:06.839 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:06.839 --> 00:05:09.241
And get this, during
a White House press conference

00:05:09.241 --> 00:05:11.110
yesterday,
Trump started talking about

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:12.845
the TV shows that he watches.

00:05:12.845 --> 00:05:15.148
It was a pretty long list.
Listen to this.

00:05:15.148 --> 00:05:17.916
-I watch some of the shows.

00:05:17.916 --> 00:05:20.086
I watch Liz McDonald.
She's fantastic.

00:05:20.086 --> 00:05:23.055
I watched Fox Business.

00:05:23.055 --> 00:05:26.159
I watched Lou Dobbs
last night,

00:05:26.159 --> 00:05:31.330
Sean Hannity last night,
Tucker last night, Laura.

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:34.467
I watched "Fox &amp; Friends"
in the morning.

00:05:35.901 --> 00:05:37.069
[ Snores ]

00:05:37.069 --> 00:05:39.639
-That's seven hours of TV
he's listed.

00:05:39.639 --> 00:05:41.374
It would have been quicker
to just name the shows

00:05:41.374 --> 00:05:43.308
on Fox News
he doesn't watch.

00:05:43.308 --> 00:05:46.312
"Everything but Chris Wallace."

00:05:46.312 --> 00:05:48.447
Yeah, at the end of every night,
Trump's TV turns to

00:05:48.447 --> 00:05:51.450
his phone and goes,
[panting] "Okay, your turn."

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:53.820
[ Laughter ]

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:55.788
Check this out.
I saw that Starbucks

00:05:55.788 --> 00:05:57.289
just made a pretty big
announcement.

00:05:57.289 --> 00:05:58.390
Listen to this.

00:05:58.390 --> 00:06:00.193 line:0%
-Starbucks is getting rid
of straws

00:06:00.193 --> 00:06:02.027 line:0%
on most of its iced drinks.

00:06:02.027 --> 00:06:03.396 line:0%
The coffee giant is rolling out

00:06:03.396 --> 00:06:07.567 line:0%
so-called sippy cup lids
for the beverages.

00:06:07.567 --> 00:06:10.169
-Here's an idea.
If you want this to catch on,

00:06:10.169 --> 00:06:13.105
maybe don't call them
sippy cups.

00:06:13.105 --> 00:06:16.408
"We got a little baby
sippy cup for Jeff?"

00:06:16.408 --> 00:06:18.444
Sippy cup for Jeff?"

00:06:18.444 --> 00:06:20.746
Meanwhile, over at Dunkin
Donuts, they'll give you a straw

00:06:20.746 --> 00:06:23.916
that comes packaged inside
two other straws.

00:06:23.916 --> 00:06:26.185
But don't worry, the plastic
straws aren't going to waste.

00:06:26.185 --> 00:06:28.320
Starbucks said that
they'll be melted down

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:30.022
and turned into breakfast
sandwiches.

00:06:30.022 --> 00:06:33.192
[ Laughter ]

00:06:33.192 --> 00:06:34.693
Here's something kind of
surprising.

00:06:34.693 --> 00:06:37.430
I heard that Oscar Mayer is
offering up its iconic

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:41.100
Wienermobile for people's
marriage proposals.

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:44.703
Here's the actual
promotional photo.

00:06:44.703 --> 00:06:46.138
Yep.

00:06:46.138 --> 00:06:48.941
Oscar Mayer says they'll
keep loaning it out

00:06:48.941 --> 00:06:51.410
until one of the proposals
ends with a yes.

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:55.314
[ Laughter ]

00:06:55.314 --> 00:06:57.183
I'm into this.
It's a great way to show

00:06:57.183 --> 00:06:59.084
your future wife
that she should be the one

00:06:59.084 --> 00:07:00.753
who handles the money.

00:07:00.753 --> 00:07:03.289
[ Laughter ]

00:07:03.289 --> 00:07:05.925
And finally, the St. Louis Zoo
says a python

00:07:05.925 --> 00:07:08.227
just laid seven eggs,
but check out

00:07:08.227 --> 00:07:09.695
why it's making headlines.

00:07:09.695 --> 00:07:12.264
-This 50-year-old python
shocked zookeepers

00:07:12.264 --> 00:07:13.966
by laying eggs.

00:07:13.966 --> 00:07:16.836
It was surprising because she
hasn't been near a male snake

00:07:16.836 --> 00:07:19.604
in 15 years.

00:07:19.604 --> 00:07:22.007
-When the news broke,
the iguana in the next exhibit

00:07:22.007 --> 00:07:24.143
was like, "Look, it was late,
we were drunk.

00:07:24.143 --> 00:07:27.913
[ Laughter ]
I'm not proud of it."

00:07:27.913 --> 00:07:29.582
Meanwhile, one zookeeper
was like,

00:07:29.582 --> 00:07:31.050
"Please don't look at the
security footage,

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:32.518
please don't look at
the security footage."

00:07:32.518 --> 00:07:33.886
-Ew!
-"Please don't look."

00:07:33.886 --> 00:07:35.555
[ Laughter ]

